# Activity 4: Group 5 Midterm Reporting – Google Docs

## Description
This activity consists of our **Group 5 Midterm Reporting** presentation slides for GE 4120 covering **Google Docs** as a cloud-based word processor[cite: 10, 27, 28]. The report explains core 21st-century document workflows—including document structure, Pages vs. Pageless formatting, collaboration permissions, Suggesting mode, Version History, Smart Chips, Citations, and Gemini AI integration—alongside an interactive quiz activity[cite: 10, 29, 35, 38, 45, 48, 51, 53, 56, 63].

## What Have I Learned?
- **Key Concepts & Skills:** I learned how Google Docs functions as a complete collaborative workflow rather than just a typing tool, particularly through structured headings, automatic tables of contents, Suggesting mode, and Version History tracking[cite: 29, 35, 37, 48, 51].
- **Challenge & Solution:** Organizing a comprehensive 63-slide deck with eight group members without overlapping content was a challenge; we solved this by dividing topics logically and using consistent retro-computer visual styling and clear section dividers[cite: 10, 27, 31].
- **Future Application & Improvement:** I can apply these Google Docs collaboration and citation features directly to nursing research papers and group case studies, and we could improve the deck by condensing text-heavy slides into more visual walkthroughs.
